# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and, with one exception,
# in the working tree too. Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true
# checks everything out as CRLF, and then:
#
#   - `pnpm format` fails on every file, because Prettier defaults to
#     endOfLine: "lf" (this was failing on 107 files locally while CI was green)
#   - shell scripts get CRLF and fail under Git Bash or WSL with the famously
#     unhelpful `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory`
#
# The exception is *.ps1: Windows PowerShell 5.1 is the documented shell for
# this repo, and CRLF is the safe convention there.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Generated, and large. Collapse them in diffs and reviews.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
packages/frontend/public/data/*.json -diff linguist-generated

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
